<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#Image> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A raster image considered as a semantic resource, with sample dimensions and interpretation supplied by the imported aspects."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#Image> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageHeader> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A structural component carrying metadata needed to interpret a raster image, separate from its pixel payload."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageHeader> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for acolor:colorSpace, araster:height, araster:width, asamp:bitDepth. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of img:ImageHeader Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Image Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#ImageShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/image> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#PixelData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The image component containing encoded or decoded sample values, distinct from header metadata."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#PixelData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity; subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#colorType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The legacy integer color-type code carried by an image header. In this vocabulary it preserves a PNG-oriented wire code, not a universal color-space identifier."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#colorType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#compressionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The legacy integer compression-method code carried by an image header; the code's interpretation is profile-specific."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#compressionMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#filterMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The legacy integer filtering-method code carried by an image header; it does not name a general-purpose semantic filter."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#filterMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#interlaceMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The legacy integer interlacing-method code carried by an image header; decode its meaning using the format profile."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/image#interlaceMethod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
